"On Stable Sector in Supermembrane Matrix Model (https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9911149)\nciteturn1academia12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 26.9 years ago; Koshelev, P. ... MedvedevDate: Thu Nov 18 23:22:21 1999 ... Energy levels are four-fold degenerate with respect to n and are labeled by n_q, the largest n in a quartet. ... We present the asymptotic solutions for the systems deriving thereby the asymptotic formula for the spectrum.\nTitle: On Stable Sector in Supermembrane Matrix Model\nAuthors: I. Ya. Aref'eva, A. S. Koshelev, P. B. Medvedev\nDate: Thu Nov 18 23:22:21 1999\n\nWe study the spectrum of SU(2) x SO(2) matrix supersymmetric quantum mechanics. We use angular coordinates that allow us to find an explicit solution of the Gauss law constraints and single out the quantum number n (the Lorentz angular momentum). Energy levels are four-fold degenerate with respect to n and are labeled by n_q, the largest n in a quartet. The Schr\\\"odinger equation is reduced to two different systems of two-dimensional partial differential equations. The choice of a system is governed by n_q. We present the asymptotic solutions for the systems deriving thereby the asymptotic formula for the spectrum. Odd n_q are forbidden, for even n_q the spectrum has a continuous part as well as a discrete one, meanwhile for half-integer n_q the spectrum is purely discrete. Taking half-integer n_q one can cure the model from instability caused by the presence of continuous spectrum.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSome analytic results concerning the mass spectrum of Yang-Mills gauge theories on a torus - ScienceDirect (https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/0550321383904364)\nciteturn1search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 43.4 years ago; Crawled: 4 weeks ago; # Some analytic results concerning the mass spectrum of Yang-Mills gauge theories on a torus☆ ... No numbers for the low-lying levels are given here, but some interesting properties of the mass spectrum already become visible.\n\n## Nuclear Physics B\n\nDate: 13 June 1983\n\nPages: 233-261\n\nVolume: Volume 219, Issue 1\n\n## Published by: Elsevier\n\nResearch article\n\nGet rights and content\n\n# Some analytic results concerning the mass spectrum of Yang-Mills gauge theories on a torus☆\n\nAuthor links open overlay panel M. Lüscher\n\n10.1016/0550-3213(83)90436-4\n\nAccess through your organizationPurchase PDF\n\nMore actions\n\n  * Article preview\n  * Recommended articles\n  * Cited by (292)\n\n## Abstract\n\nWhen non-abelian gauge fields are enclosed in a box with periodic boundary conditions, the spectrum of the hamiltonian becomes discrete and the energy values can be expanded in a power series of . A method to obtain these expansions is explained and worked out to one-loop order. No numbers for the low-lying levels are given here, but some interesting properties of the mass spectrum already become visible.\n\n## References (11)\n\n  * M. Lüscher\n\n### Phys. Lett.\n\n(1982)\n\n  * G. 't Hooft et al.\n\n### Nucl. Phys.\n\n(1972)\n\nG. 't Hooft\n\n### Nucl. Phys.\n\n(1973)\n\n  * C. Bloch\n\n### Nucl. Phys.\n\n(1958)\n\n  * J.D. Bjorken\n\n### Elements of quantum chromodynamics\n\n  * A. Gonzalez-Arroyo et al.\n\n### Ground state metamorphosis for Yang-Mills fields on a finite periodic lattice\n\nThere are more references available in the full text version of this article.\n\n^{☆}\n    \n\nWork in part supported by Schweizerischer Nationalfonds.\n\nView full text--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nB. Simon's Publications (https://math.caltech.edu/simon/biblio.html)\nciteturn1search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 months ago; SIMON'S COMPLETE LIST OF PUBLICATIONS ... ### Note:  The button marked Image: art.gif (1199 bytes) provides a pdf of the article for your personal, non-commercial use and should not be reposted. ... Rosen) The P(φ)_{2} Euclidean quantum field theory as classical statis